Q1. Create N children and display cumulative user & kernel time
============================================================

Question:
Write a program to create 'n' children. When the children terminate,
display total cumulative time children spent in user and kernel mode.

#include<stdio.h>
#include<unistd.h>
#include<sys/wait.h>
#include<sys/resource.h>

int main()
{
    int n,i;
    struct rusage r;

    printf("Enter number of children: ");
    scanf("%d",&n);

    for(i=0;i<n;i++)
        if(fork()==0) return 0;

    for(i=0;i<n;i++) wait(NULL);

    getrusage(RUSAGE_CHILDREN,&r);

    printf("User Time   : %ld.%06ld sec\n",r.ru_utime.tv_sec,r.ru_utime.tv_usec);
    printf("Kernel Time : %ld.%06ld sec\n",r.ru_stime.tv_sec,r.ru_stime.tv_usec);

    return 0;
}

1-LINE EXPLANATIONS:
fork()        - Creates a new child process.
wait()        - Makes the parent wait until a child terminates.
getrusage()   - Gets resource usage information of the process/children.
RUSAGE_CHILDREN - Specifies that resource usage of terminated children is required.
ru_utime      - Gives the cumulative CPU time spent by children in user mode.
ru_stime      - Gives the cumulative CPU time spent by children in kernel/system mode.
scanf()       - Takes N, the number of children, as user input.

IMPORTANT NOTE:
The PDF asks for cumulative user and kernel time in Q1, but the provided
PDF does not explicitly list getrusage(); it lists getrlimit(), which is
a different function. getrusage() is used here because it provides the
CPU-time values required by the question.

