Q2. Demonstrate atexit()
============================================================

Question:
Write a program to demonstrate the use of atexit() function.

#include<stdio.h>
#include<stdlib.h>

void fun()
{
    printf("atexit() function executed\n");
}

int main()
{
    atexit(fun);
    printf("Inside main()\n");
    return 0;
}

OUTPUT:
Inside main()
atexit() function executed

1-LINE EXPLANATIONS:
atexit()      - Registers a function that executes when the program terminates normally.
fun()         - The function registered with atexit().
return 0      - Normally terminates main(), causing the registered atexit() function to run.

